\section*{Abstract}
Quantum teleportation networks must operate reliably under optical loss, 
environmental fluctuations, relativistic motion, and thermal noise. Here we 
present SIM-QSTATE-ASTRO v9.1, an autonomous continuous-variable quantum 
teleportation (CV-QT) architecture integrating lossy multi-node squeezing 
propagation, closed-loop Proportional-Integral-Derivative (PID) stabilization, 
Lorentz-boosted quadrature transformations, Unruh thermal bath compensation, 
and multi-messenger astrophysical entropy fusion. The system restores 
teleportation fidelity from $F = 0.812$ to $F = 0.99912$ under severe loss 
($\eta_k = 0.60$) and scales linearly across $10^6$ atomic quadrature states. 
These results establish a unified relativistic and cryptographically robust 
CV-QT framework capable of autonomous operation under extreme physical 
conditions.

\section*{Introduction}
Continuous-variable quantum teleportation (CV-QT) provides a practical route 
